{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame\/halign","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"The most typical case is for credits, such as:"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlframe\/halign"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"halign","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Words and music by Pat Songwriter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Typically this type of credit is aligned to the right, so that the position information refers to the right-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most part of the text. But in this example, the text is center-justified, not right-justified."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The halign attribute is used in these situations. If it is not present, its value is the same as for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"justify attribute. For elements where a justify attribute is not allowed, the default is implementation-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"code":"halign","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","title":"halign","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"halign"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLFrameV6halignAA18MXLLeftCenterRightOSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFrame/halign":{"title":"halign","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"halign","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLLeftCenterRightO","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify values can be different.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The most typical case is for credits, such as:"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame\/halign","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlframe\/halign"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFrame":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The frame type represents a frame or fretboard diagram used together with a chord symbol. The representation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is based on the NIFF guitar grid with additional information. The frame type’s unplayed attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"what to display above a string that has no associated frame-note element. Typical values are x and the empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"string. If the attribute is not present, the display of the unplayed string is application-defined."}],"title":"MXLFrame","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFrame"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFrame"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlframe","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLeftCenterRight":{"title":"MXLLeftCenterRight","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"MXLLeftCenterRight","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlleftcenterright","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLeftCenterRight","abstract":[{"text":"The left-center-right type is used to define horizontal alignment and text justification.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLeftCenterRight"}]}}}